  "prediction": "The report examines the safety and health of workers in the meat and poultry industry, focusing on the efforts of the Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) to ensure compliance with regulations. The report finds that while OSHA has made progress in reducing injuries and illnesses in the industry, there are still challenges, including a high rate of foreign-born workers who may not be fully aware of their rights or the hazards they face. The report also highlights the need for better communication and coordination between OSHA, employers, and workers to address these issues. Additionally, the report discusses the challenges of enforcing safety regulations in large, complex processing plants and the importance of ongoing training and education for workers. The report recommends that OSHA continue to prioritize enforcement efforts in the meat and poultry industry, while also working to improve outreach and education to workers and employers. Overall, the report emphasizes the importance of ensuring that all workers in the industry are aware of their rights and the hazards they face, and that employers are providing a safe and healthy working environment.",
  "scored_prediction": "The report examines the safety and health of workers in the meat and poultry industry, focusing on the efforts of the Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) to ensure compliance with regulations. The report finds that while OSHA has made progress in reducing injuries and illnesses in the industry, there are still challenges, including a high rate of foreign-born workers who may not be fully aware of their rights or the hazards they face. The report also highlights the need for better communication and coordination between OSHA, employers, and workers to address these issues. Additionally, the report discusses the challenges of enforcing safety regulations in large, complex processing plants and the importance of ongoing training and education for workers. The report recommends that OSHA continue to prioritize enforcement efforts in the meat and poultry industry, while also working to improve outreach and education to workers and employers. Overall, the report emphasizes the importance of ensuring that all workers in the industry are aware of their rights and the hazards they face, and that employers are providing a safe and healthy working environment.",
